# logaperture-sample-quarkus endpoints -- the dev/quarkus target.
#
# Needs the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): a "Send Request" link
# appears above each request below. Bring the app up first:
#
#   python3 dev/quarkus/quarkusctl.py up
#
# The answer reports what each logger will emit (trace=, debug=, julFine=, floor=);
# the log lines themselves go to the app's output: `quarkusctl tail`.
#
# There is no timer endpoint (spec decision QD4). To watch a `for 2m` expiry,
#   watch -n 5 curl -s 'localhost:8081/log?tag=watch'

@base = http://localhost:8081

### Every level through JBoss Logging and java.util.logging.
GET {{base}}/log

### Tagged, so the lines are easy to find in the output.
GET {{base}}/log?tag=x

### 50 repeats of a line (for drop and trim rules, and `logctl top`).
GET {{base}}/log?tag=x&repeat=50
